4.1                      mcfost version

#Number of photon packages
  128000    nbr_photons_eq_th  : T computation
  128000    nbr_photons_lambda : SED computation
  128000    nbr_photons_image  : images computation

#Wavelength
  50  0.1 3000.0          n_lambda, lambda_min, lambda_max [mum] Do not change this line unless you know what you are doing
  F  F  T    compute temperature?, compute sed?, use default wavelength grid for output ?
  wavelength.lambda    wavelength file (if previous parameter is F)
  T  T    separation of different contributions?, stokes parameters?

#Grid geometry and size
  2                       1 = cylindrical, 2 = spherical (spherical is MANDATORY when a zone is an envelope)
  100  70  1  20    n_rad (log distribution), nz (or n_theta), n_az, n_rad_in

#Maps
  2401  2401  6000    grid (nx,ny), size [AU]
  60  60  1  F    RT: imin, imax, n_incl, centered ?
  0    0.   1             RT: az_min, az_max, n_az angles
  140    distance (pc)
  0.                      disk PA

#Scattering method
  1                       1=exact phase function, 2=hg function with same g (2 implies the loss of polarizarion)

#Symmetries
  F    image symmetry
  T                       central symmetry
  T                       axial symmetry (important only if N_phi > 1)

#Disk physics
  0     0.50  1.0         dust_settling (0=no settling, 1=parametric, 2=Dubrulle, 3=Fromang), exp_strat, a_strat (for parametric settling)
  F                       dust radial migration
  F                       sublimate dust
  F                       hydostatic equilibrium
  F  1e-5                 viscous heating, alpha_viscosity

#Number of zones : 1 zone = 1 density structure + corresponding grain properties
  2                       needs to be 1 if you read a density file (phantom or fits file)

#Density structure
  1                       ZONE 1 - zone type : 1 = disk, 2 = tappered-edge disk, 3 = envelope, 4 = debris disk, 5 = wall
  1.e-4    100.           dust mass,  gas-to-dust mass ratio
  10.  100.0  2           scale height, reference radius (AU), unused for envelope, vertical profile exponent (only for debris disk)
  0.3  0.0    100.  100.  Rin, edge, Rout, Rc (AU) Rc is only used for tappered-edge & debris disks (Rout set to 8*Rc if Rout==0)
  1.125                   flaring exponent, unused for envelope
  -1.0  0.0               surface density exponent (or -gamma for tappered-edge disk or volume density for envelope), usually < 0, -gamma_exp (or alpha_in & alpha_out for debris disk)

  3                       ZONE 2 - zone type : 1 = disk, 2 = tappered-edge disk, 3 = envelope, 4 = debris disk, 5 = wall
  0.000225  100.0    dust mass,  gas-to-dust mass ratio
  10.  100.0  2           scale height, reference radius (AU), unused for envelope, vertical profile exponent (only for debris disk)
  1.0  0.0    3000. 100.  Rin, edge, Rout, Rc (AU) Rc is only used for tappered-edge & debris disks (Rout set to 8*Rc if Rout==0)
  1.125                   flaring exponent, unused for envelope
  -1.5  0.0               surface density exponent (or -gamma for tappered-edge disk or volume density for envelope), usually < 0, -gamma_exp (or alpha_in & alpha_out for debris disk)

#Grain properties
  2  Number of species                                    ZONE 1 : bare, grown grains in the disk
  Mie  1 1  0.0  0.7  0.9 Grain type (Mie or DHS), N_components, mixing rule (1 = EMT or 2 = coating),  porosity, mass fraction, Vmax (for DHS)
  Draine_Si_sUV.dat  1.0  Optical indices file, volume fraction
  1                       Heating method : 1 = RE + LTE, 2 = RE + NLTE, 3 = NRE
  0.03  1000.0  3.5  50    amin, amax [mum], aexp, n_grains (log distribution)

  Mie  1 1  0.0  0.3  0.9 Grain type (Mie or DHS), N_components, mixing rule (1 = EMT or 2 = coating),  porosity, mass fraction, Vmax (for DHS)
  ac_opct.dat        1.0  Optical indices file, volume fraction   (Rouleau & Martin 1991)
  1                       Heating method : 1 = RE + LTE, 2 = RE + NLTE, 3 = NRE
  0.03  1000.0  3.5  50    amin, amax [mum], aexp, n_grains (log distribution)

  1  Number of species                                    ZONE 2 : ice-coated grains in the envelope
  Mie  2 2  0.0  1.0  0.9 Grain type (Mie or DHS), N_components, mixing rule (1 = EMT or 2 = coating),  porosity, mass fraction, Vmax (for DHS)
  Draine_Si_sUV.dat  0.95    Optical indices file, volume fraction  (core)
  ice_opct.dat  0.05    Optical indices file, volume fraction  (mantle)
  1                       Heating method : 1 = RE + LTE, 2 = RE + NLTE, 3 = NRE
  0.03  0.4  2.75  50    amin, amax [mum], aexp, n_grains (log distribution)

#Molecular RT settings
  T T T                   lpop, laccurate_pop, LTE
  0.05 cs                 Turbulence velocity, unit km/s or cs
  1                       Number of molecules
  co.dat 6                molecular data filename, level max up to which NLTE populations are calculated
  T 1.e-4 abundance.fits.gz   cst molecule abundance ?, abundance, abundance file
  T  2                       ray tracing ?,  number of lines in ray-tracing
  2 3                     transition numbers
  -10.0 10.0 41           vmin and vmax [km/s], number of velocity bins betwen vmin and vmax

#Atoms settings / share some informations with molecules
 1              number of atoms
 H_6.atom       all levels treated in details at the moment
 F              non-LTE ?
 0              initial solution, 0 LTE, 1 from file
 1000 101       vmax (km/s), n_points for ray-traced images and total flux
 T 1            images (T) or total flux (F) ? Number of lines for images
 3 2            upper level -> lower level (Atomic model dependent)

#Star properties
 1 Number of stars
  4000  2.5  0.5  0.0  0.0  0.0  T    Temp, radius (solar radius),M (solar mass),x,y,z (AU), automatic spectrum?
 lte4000-3.5.NextGen.fits.gz
 0.0    2.2  fUV, slope_fUV
